# Theme Color Modes

Figma (EISCO Main variables) is the **structure** SSOT: two axes + semantic roles. Implementation names in this repo’s `_styles/` can lag Figma — **grep `_styles/` before coding** and use what exists. Names below are **illustrative**.

## Two axes (Figma)

1. **Section tone** (`02.02 Base/Colors` modes): `primary` | `secondary` | `muted` | `accent` | `contrast` | `elevated`.
   Put the matching mode class on the **section root**. New Figma-driven themes use this **six-tone** set — a single `accent` tone, **not** `accent-1` / `accent-2` / `accent-3`.
2. **Brand vertical** (`01.02 Theme/Brand` modes): `education` | `industrial` when the theme has it.
   Optional second root / `html` class. Children still use semantic roles only.

**Older `_styles/`:** some themes still ship `color-schema-accent-1|2|3` and omit `elevated`. Use the utilities grep finds. Do not invent `color-schema-elevated` or collapse accent-1/2/3 unless this theme defines the new set. Do not treat accent-1/2/3 as the Figma SSOT.

## Two layers

1. **Primitives / brand scales** (`01.01 Theme/Primitives`, `01.02 Theme/Brand`) — raw ramps (`color/neutral/*`, `color/accent/*`, `color/brand/*` 50–950), fonts, radii. CSS-only. Never as Liquid Tailwind classes.
2. **Semantic roles** (`02.02 Base/Colors` aliases into Brand). When present in `_styles/`, Liquid uses:
   - **bg:** `surface` | `subtle` | `emphasis` | `accent` | `accent-sec`
   - **text:** `primary` | `secondary` | `accent` | `on-accent` | `on-accent-sec`
   - **border:** `primary` | `secondary` | `tertiary` | `accent` | `on-accent` | `on-accent-sec`

`02.03 Base/Alphacolors` (`0-*` overlays) is **legacy** — do not use as the primary color API.

If `_styles/` is missing a Figma role (e.g. `text-accent`, `bg-accent-sec`, `border-tertiary`), do **not** invent the class or fall back to hex. Use the closest shipped semantic utility, or add the token in a theme `_styles` PR.

## Mode first

1. Read Figma / schema for **tone** (six-tone set above) and, if used, **brand vertical**.
2. Grep `_styles/` for `@utility`, `color-schema-*`, brand-vertical classes, and semantic `@theme` roles.
3. Put tone (and brand, when present) on the **section root** (or the wrapper this theme documents).
4. Children use **only semantic utilities**. The mode remaps those tokens — do not restyle children with primitives or hex to “match Figma.”

## Size modes

- **Layout density** (`02.01 Base/Sizes`): `lg` | `md` | `default` → responsive utilities (`md:`, `lg:`) and size tokens — never hard `px` or `text-[14px]`.
- **Component density** (`03.01 Components/Sizes`): `lg` | `base` | `sm` — use this theme’s component size utilities when present.
- **Component color** (`03.02 Components/Colors`): `primary` | `secondary` — component-level, still semantic; not a substitute for section tone.

## Forbidden

- Arbitrary hex / rgb in Tailwind: `text-[#d1d1d1]`, `bg-[#fff]`, `border-[rgb(...)]`
- Inventing token or utility names that do not exist in `_styles/`
- Building class names with Liquid: `text-{{ color }}`, `bg-{{ settings.color }}`
- Primitive / brand-scale classes in Liquid (`text-neutral-400`, `bg-accent-700`, old named ramps)
- Teaching `accent-1|2|3` as the Figma tone list

## Discovery (do this before coding)

```bash
rg -n "@utility|color-schema|--background-color|--text-color|--border-color|@theme|education|industrial|elevated" _styles/
```

Typical homes (paths vary): `_styles/02_base/*colors*.css`, `_styles/01_theme/*`, `_styles/main.css`.

Then read `figma-design-system.mdc` (7 collections) and `tailwindcss-rules.mdc` (static classes, `@source`).

## Illustrative only

```liquid
<section class="color-schema-muted">
  <div class="bg-surface text-primary border-secondary">
    <h2 class="text-primary">…</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary">…</p>
    <a class="text-accent">…</a>
  </div>
</section>
```

`color-schema-muted`, `bg-surface`, `text-primary`, and `text-accent` are Figma-shaped examples. Replace them with utilities this theme actually defines in `_styles/`.
